{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack","id":603548,"title":"[Beast] Horror Form Hack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-25T23:38:51-07:00","id":603548,"title":"[Beast] Horror Form Hack","content":"I see there are many STs like me that likes all or most of the Beast material, but they lack one, crucial thing in the Begotten as they are \u2013 ability for changing your human body in to Horror you have inside, even for a while. So here I give you mine idea on the topic \u2013 I would also gladly listen to yours takes on subject.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Horror Form Ability</b><br /> In times of great stress and great need, the Beasts can shed a human body they have for a short while to become living embodiment of Horror they have inside themselves. But it comes with great costs to them. Not only they are clearly visible for what they are, they becoming Hunger incarnate and by this are prone to summon Heroes to kill them. That\u2019s a cost of Horror\u2019s true power.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b><br /> Beast Character can shed her human form for one scene ( or 1 hour, whatever is shorter ) and take a form of her Horror, limited in the Size to her normal ratings \u2013 she become monstrous being Begotten is inside on the outside. For the time being she has activated all the Atavisms and Birthrights she has bought without any Satiety Expenditure. If some Atavisms or Merits made here larger or smaller they are also taken in consideration in Horror Form.<br /> <br /> But there is price for the unleashing the Horror inside on the outside. Beside clearly visible monstrous nature to everyone around, character lose any points of Satiety it had and is automatically in Ravenous Condition. She also summons the Heroes, on normal rules for event of Satiety 0.</span></span><br /> <br /> This is all I have for now. I also thought about variant with Horror Form for the Lair numbers in turn and costing only Lair number of Satiety points, but I feel the \u201call in for monstrous Hunger\u201d is much better solution \u2013 akin to Death Rage of werewolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you like it? Are there some omissions to the rules that need to be stated or cleared?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-26-2015, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T23:44:54-07:00","id":603564,"title":"","content":"Should the Atavisms not receive the benefits of Satiety Expenditure in Horror Form? I'm on the fence, because while it's certainly hilariously overpowered to give the Satiety Expenditure benefits, this certainly seems like a &quot;Shit Just Got Real&quot; button, which seems like an appropriate time for going full Monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T11:56:32-07:00","id":603988,"title":"","content":"I really like this. I think that Malonkey has a good point, both for and against the benefits/balance issues of Satiety Expenditure. If I were to do this myself, I think I would probably shoe in something like, &quot;If the Beast was at Satiety 5+ at the time of activation, she may choose one Atavism to recieve the benefits of Satiety Expenditure for the remainder of the Scene. Additionally, since the Transformation itself requires the expenditure of all Satiety points, treat ALL manifested Atavisms besides the players' choice Atavism as Low Satiety.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something like that. Maybe. Haven't playtested it, but it sounds cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:06:00-07:00","id":603992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=603988#post603988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this. I think that Malonkey has a good point, both for and against the benefits/balance issues of Satiety Expenditure. If I were to do this myself, I think I would probably shoe in something like, &quot;If the Beast was at Satiety 5+ at the time of activation, she may choose one Atavism to recieve the benefits of Satiety Expenditure for the remainder of the Scene. Additionally, since the Transformation itself requires the expenditure of all Satiety points, treat ALL manifested Atavisms besides the players' choice Atavism as Low Satiety.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something like that. Maybe. Haven't playtested it, but it sounds cool.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds reasonable to me. And agreed, this is a crisp and clean guideline for this important yet missing feature. I've read that the developers shied away from including a Horror Form because they thought it would step on the toes of Demonic Form, but that might not be true.<br /> <br /> I would also say that you may cap the time you can spend in Horror Form with Lair in some way. Or say it lasts for the remainder of the scene and can only be used once per chapter. Any combination which fits your desired power level is valid. Just be mindful of Heroes that know <a href=\"http://pt.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Ganking\" target=\"_blank\">gank-fu</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-26-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:50:28-07:00","id":604085,"title":"","content":"So for now, Horror Form is usable once per chapter and has those powers for the scene:<ul><li>All Atavisms of Beast are active at Low Satiety variant.</li> <li>If character were having Satiety 5+ on activating Horror Form, one Atavism works as with Statiety Expendetiture.</li> <li>Beast lose here all the Satiety and is in Ravenous Condition.</li> </ul>Does this sound balanced and potent enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-26-2015, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:55:44-07:00","id":604123,"title":"","content":"It sounds extremely potent, but worrisome enough that I would hesitate to use it.<br /> <br /> edit: And that's a good thing. Not sure if it's balanced, persay. Others would be better at weighing that than I would. Sounds cool as hell though, and is exactly the thing that would bring all elements of Beast into glorious harmony, at least for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 07-26-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T14:49:37-07:00","id":604191,"title":"","content":"I find it thematically proper. In every monster tale, usually the monsters pull this in the last scene, when the heroes come for the final fight. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/opmvt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T03:55:10-07:00","id":604580,"title":"","content":"Ummm..... <br /> <br /> What exactly does this do other than make your Horror visible to mundane people? It sounds like what I do all the time with a Starving character as is, and that's without falling into Ravenous Condition. If anything, this sounds like a disadvantage, since you're more likely to make Heroes show up, and that makes everyone else upset with you. No one likes hunters in their backyard, and that's exactly what you'd be doing. <br /> <br /> Wyrdhamster, you asked if this &quot;balanced and potent enough?&quot; I fail to see any advantages to this at all - you're moving right into Ravenous (avoiding the chance for Beats from resolving other Conditions on your way down), have the same mechanical benefits as if you were merely Starving, drawing more heroes and hunters to you and your brood mates and kin through exposure, have no Satiety to employ the more potent powers, will have trouble regaining Satiety after the scene ends, no access to Low Satiety effects after scene ends. That's pure disadvantage. <br /> <br /> At best, the only advantage I can see is using the Power/Finesse/Resilience spread, and, even then? That minor bonus pales in comparison to the Low Satiety effects of Atavisms. Plus, if you open a Primordial Pathway while Starving, you get Lair bonus to your Power when going that way.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm missing something, this is neither balanced, nor potent. Its a trap. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T06:31:55-07:00","id":604636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=604580#post604580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ummm.....<br /> <br /> What exactly does this do other than make your Horror visible to mundane people? It sounds like what I do all the time with a Starving character as is, and that's without falling into Ravenous Condition. If anything, this sounds like a disadvantage, since you're more likely to make Heroes show up, and that makes everyone else upset with you. No one likes hunters in their backyard, and that's exactly what you'd be doing.<br /> <br /> Wyrdhamster, you asked if this &quot;balanced and potent enough?&quot; </div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are right. Seeing how the mechanics works now version is only trouble.<br /> <br /> But here is mine answer - <b>How would it work if you get from Horror Form all your Atavisms with Satiety Expenditure effects plus all the previous powers? </b>With instant turn on at least 3 Atavisms with higher forms I think it's more pleasing version.<br /> <br /> As to Horrors higher statistics - it interesting idea, but I do not want to overpower the Horror Form ability. What do you think guys - <b>Should Beasts use higher stats in Horror Form beside all the previous powers?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T06:53:24-07:00","id":604672,"title":"","content":"Yes? If we're using the form of the Horror we should be using its stats for our physical scores. Also I think using the Form should Only cost us Satiety as if we were activating our Atavisms in the first place. Maybe only let it be usable at low satiety so that it has more likely hood of actually pushing us towards 0. Say because at higher satiety our Horror is already less prone to giving us stronger atavisms, it is also less likely to want to come out of the lair at all. (At high satiety its becoming lazy and sluggish as it is.)<br /> <br /> Edit: Oooo maybe double the satiety cost on the first 1 or 2 atavisms activated with the form if you're using it from High Satiety, call it enticing the horror. Also thought, maybe tie said stats to the number of atavisms used, somehow....<br /> <br /> Edit 2: X3 If you're using it from high you're gonna feel the burn, if you're using it from Low you're gonna be slipping closer and closer to that edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 07-27-2015, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T07:29:22-07:00","id":604688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=604636#post604636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here is mine answer - <b>How would it work if you get from Horror Form all your Atavisms with Satiety Expenditure effects plus all the previous powers?</b></div> </div> </div> </div> That would be too much. Even the Horror can't do that on its own turf in the Lair. Doing it while merged is a bit excessive. I mean, some of the Atavisms are scene long, but others are per-turn. Turning those perma-on feels off to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With instant turn on at least 3 Atavisms with higher forms I think it's more pleasing version. </div> </div> </div> Eh... If I'm holding out at Satiety 4, and activate 3 Atavaisms, I'm still at the same advantage while only Starving, plus I get a Beat for resolving Sated. If I had 7 Satiety, I could activate 4 Atavisms and be only Starving, plus have three Satiety left over and get 2 beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to Horrors higher statistics - it interesting idea, but I do not want to overpower the Horror Form ability. What do you think guys - <b>Should Beasts use higher stats in Horror Form beside all the previous powers?</b> </div> </div> </div> You get it from opening a Primordial Pathway and merging with your Beast. Not having it here is exceedingly strange. (( For the record, getting an exceptional success on opening a Primordial Pathway lets you merge with the Horror for the full scene as well, giving the same visual and mechanical result as your hack. ))<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T08:25:24-07:00","id":604740,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting idea. I think I would limit like a Werewolf's Gauru form, with regards to duration. So something like 1 turn / Satiety spent + 1 turn / dot of Lair instead of the entire scene.<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;trap&quot; feature that MCN speaks of is okay. If anything, I'd double down on it. The Beast will stop and gorge on anything it kills in this form (may still defend itself from attacks), gaining one point of Satiety for every 10 pounds of flesh consumed, stopping only when Satiety 10 has been achieved or the &quot;kill&quot; has been entirely consumed. It then flees the scene, searching for a secluded spot to sleep in. The Beast reawakens as a human after 10 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T08:33:18-07:00","id":604742,"title":"","content":"It might also make sense if you had to superimpose your lair over the area, thus limiting the ability to &quot;home&quot; territory. Could make the get away easier (escape into Lair) which should be balanced with another cost (you sleep in your lair you attract the Astral equivalent of vermin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T02:34:25-07:00","id":700576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=604688#post604688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You get it from opening a Primordial Pathway and merging with your Beast. Not having it here is exceedingly strange. (( For the record, getting an exceptional success on opening a Primordial Pathway lets you merge with the Horror for the full scene as well, giving the same visual and mechanical result as your hack. ))</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps an alternative to Wyrdhamster's hack would be a Merit that lets Beasts get an Exceptional Success with 3 successes instead of 5 when opening Primordial Pathways. This Merit would be rated from 2 to 4 dots, and would let Beasts ignore a number of penalties to the Wits + Resolve roll equal to its dot rating - 1. Add a Lair prerequisite of 3 or 4 and we're good to go. Let's not forget that Beasts who impose their Lair and thus merge with their Horrors can spend willpower points in place of Satiety to improve Atavisms (but they cannot use Nightmares). Furthermore, if the Horror's total Willpower dots are greater than the Beast's Willpower dots, a number of temporary Willpower points equal to the difference between the two would be gained.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-14-2015, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T09:55:08-07:00","id":701037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=700576#post700576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps an alternative to Wyrdhamster's hack would be a Merit that lets Beasts get an Exceptional Success with 3 successes instead of 5 when opening Primordial Pathways. This Merit would be rated from 2 to 4 dots, and would let Beasts ignore a number of penalties to the Wits + Resolve roll equal to the its dot rating - 1. Add a Lair prerequisite of 3 or 4 and we're good to go. Let's not forget that Beasts who impose their Lair and thus merge with their Horrors can spend willpower points in place of Satiety to improve Atavisms (but they cannot use Nightmares). Furthermore, if the Horror's total Willpower dots are greater than the Beast's Willpower dots, a number of temporary Willpower points equal to the difference between the two would be gained.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a happy medium to me, although the Willpower thing is a little wonky to me.<br /> <br /> A merit that allows the narrative Resonance of a location where you draw down your Lair to bleed into the surrounding area could also be useful. Have the location be functionally identical to a Locus with a rating equal to half the Lair Trait of the Begotten that did the drawing, with a penalty based upon its Narrative Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:36:01-07:00","id":701173,"title":"","content":"How I miss this when it was posted? Regardless I like it, I was already considering something like this and yours is a good jumping point. So I'll be using it, slightly tweaked.<br /> <br /> Tweaked Version:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Mythic Form </b><br /> In times of great stress, great need, or great hunger Beasts can shed their human body to become living embodiment of horror they have inside themselves. Albeit at great cost. To invoke this form the Beast must expend all her remaining Satiety, taking the Ravenous Condition, and cannot gain further Satiety for the remainder of the scene. Beasts who expend all their Satiety normally are at risk of assuming this form involuntarily. Any time a Beast with the Ravenous Conditions encounters a stimulus for their Hunger they must roll their remaining unspent willpower points, on a failure they assume their Mythic Form.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: In Mythic Form a Beast becomes the physical embodiment of her internal soul. Her true form and Atavisms become visible to onlookers, while her human body fades from sight. While in this form the Beast uses her Mythic Traits* (see note below), and treats all Atavisms as though she had spent Satiety to power them. However, this power comes at a price. For one the Beast must simplemindedly pursue her Hunter, ignoring all other interests. This isn't like Death Rage or Frenzy, the Beast retains her sentience, ability to reason, plot and even converse, but she cares for nothing save the sating of her thirsts. Second, the Beast becomes a magnet for Heroes, like a sixth sense heroes from all over the land will feel the pull to hunt her. Mythic Form lasts until the end of the scene, or until the Beast flees into her Lair.<br /> <br /> *<b>Note</b>: Further hacks modify the Beast's True Form with the following statistics:<ul><li>The Horror, instead of gaining [Lair * 2] points to spend between her Attributes and size, adds her Lair dots to all Dice Pools, her Size, Defense, Initiative, and Speed. Applies her full defense vs Firearms, and cannot suffer Conditions that make no sense in her new form, like Arm Wrack on a giant snake. (No longer must Beasts labor under dubious to downright embarrassingly low dice pools)</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 10-14-2015, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:44:57-07:00","id":701177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701173#post701173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They use Spirit Attributes, calculating Power, Finesse and Resolve using the highest Attribute in the relevant category. (No longer must Beasts specialize in the mental spread for power)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is already the case for the Horror's Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:52:14-07:00","id":701179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701177#post701177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is already the case for the Horror's Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thank god. I see now I slightly misread that section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:42:15-07:00","id":701347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701173#post701173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For one the Beast must simplemindedly pursue her Hunter, ignoring all other interests.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;My interest is to hold off this rampaging Werewolf from killing my friends. But if I reveal my full form, I have to go collect shiny gemstones instead of protecting my kin.&quot; Waste all your Satiety to... just do things to eat more? Almost entirely pointless except in niche situations and very specific Hungers. Feeding your Hunger isn't the whole of the game, so having that be the only concern will be vastly meaningless for doing any number of other things. Also, remember that feeding your Hunger up from Ravenous requires the same dedication as if you were at Satiety 8 - as in, requiring exceedingly elaborate set ups over the course of a very long period of time, or a very specific and rare appearance that will be difficult to track down. This means that, once you &quot;simplemindedly&quot; goes after their Hunger, we're talking about immediate abandonment of the rest of the brood in search of that very specific thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, the Beast becomes a magnet for Heroes, like a sixth sense heroes from all over the land will feel the pull to hunt her. Mythic Form lasts until the end of the scene, or until the Beast flees into her Lair. </div> </div> </div> And suicidal as well. So, not only are you stuck in Ravenous literally <i>dying from hunger, </i>but you have hunters on your tail ready to kill you when you're at your weakest (No Satiety to spend, can't regain it except in one way, no Low Satiety benefits). Seriously, Ravenous is equivalent to becoming one of Cover 0 Burned in DtD without any aether to spend. It takes an entire session just focusing on getting something to keep the Beast in question from dying naturally. And that's a struggle with the full PC party focused on &quot;nursing&quot; you back to health. Remember - Satiety isn't a fuel stat like vitae. Its your fuel combined with Integrity-equivalent. Hitting 0 in any Integrity-equivalent is very bad.<br /> <br /> This has massive, massive RP considerations beyond just flashing someone your form. It dominates the entire direction of the game for several sessions, as well as risking everyone's lives. Might be fun once or twice, but it will get stale, quick, akin to role playing through every single feeding scene in Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]The Horror, instead of gaining [Lair * 2] points to spend between her Attributes and size, adds her Lair dots to all Dice Pools, her Size, Defense, Initiative, and Speed. Applies her full defense vs Firearms, and cannot suffer Conditions that make no sense in her new form, like Arm Wrack on a giant snake. (No longer must Beasts labor under dubious to downright embarrassingly low dice pools) </div> </div> </div> *rubs eyes* First of all, you already have that immunity to tilts and conditions like that from Atavisms. If you have a form that would logically be immune, then you'd have the appropriate Atavism for it already, or getting it soon. Granted, there's no good &quot;snake form&quot; abilities yet (strange for a Family that supposedly has Gorgons), but that's another matter entirely - there are already ways we're covering this.<br /> <br /> Secondly, embarassing low dice pools? Has that really been the experience? I can't say I have seen it. Atavisms generally grant significant bonuses to mundane rolls and not use rolls to activate. Nightmares have Satiety as part of the roll, which use Satiety, which can be a very large number easily.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, there's a bit of disconnect here. Not everyone is a giant powerful creature of doom. A siren shouldn't be suddenly a powerful, large combatant. Adding Lair to Size makes no sense here. Not all monsters make sense to gain bonus Defense or Initiative, as they're not a swift form. Gaining bonuses to social and intelectual abilities is likewise very strange in a number of cases. Just... why? Also, adds Lair to resistance rolls twice?<br /> <br /> Fourth, this mechanically not that different from simply spending the required Satiety to empower your abilities. The only benefit is &quot;flashing&quot; your form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-14-2015, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T16:43:18-07:00","id":701409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701347#post701347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;My interest is to hold off this rampaging Werewolf from killing my friends. But if I reveal my full form, I have to go collect shiny gemstones instead of protecting my kin.&quot; Waste all your Satiety to... just do things to eat more? Almost entirely pointless except in niche situations and very specific Hungers. Feeding your Hunger isn't the whole of the game, so having that be the only concern will be vastly meaningless for doing any number of other things. Also, remember that feeding your Hunger up from Ravenous requires the same dedication as if you were at Satiety 8 - as in, requiring exceedingly elaborate set ups over the course of a very long period of time, or a very specific and rare appearance that will be difficult to track down. This means that, once you &quot;simplemindedly&quot; goes after their Hunger, we're talking about immediate abandonment of the rest of the brood in search of that very specific thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, fair point. Should revise that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701347#post701347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And suicidal as well. So, not only are you stuck in Ravenous literally <i>dying from hunger, </i>but you have hunters on your tail ready to kill you when you're at your weakest (No Satiety to spend, can't regain it except in one way, no Low Satiety benefits). Seriously, Ravenous is equivalent to becoming one of Cover 0 Burned in DtD without any aether to spend. It takes an entire session just focusing on getting something to keep the Beast in question from dying naturally. And that's a struggle with the full PC party focused on &quot;nursing&quot; you back to health. Remember - Satiety isn't a fuel stat like vitae. Its your fuel combined with Integrity-equivalent. Hitting 0 in any Integrity-equivalent is very bad.<br /> <br /> This has massive, massive RP considerations beyond just flashing someone your form. It dominates the entire direction of the game for several sessions, as well as risking everyone's lives. Might be fun once or twice, but it will get stale, quick, akin to role playing through every single feeding scene in Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, it's not supposed to be something done trivially. Going Loud is a good comparison, a terrible idea, but there if you need it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701347#post701347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*rubs eyes* First of all, you already have that immunity to tilts and conditions like that from Atavisms. If you have a form that would logically be immune, then you'd have the appropriate Atavism for it already, or getting it soon. Granted, there's no good &quot;snake form&quot; abilities yet (strange for a Family that supposedly has Gorgons), but that's another matter entirely - there are already ways we're covering this.<br /> <br /> Secondly, embarassing low dice pools? Has that really been the experience? I can't say I have seen it. Atavisms generally grant significant bonuses to mundane rolls and not use rolls to activate. Nightmares have Satiety as part of the roll, which use Satiety, which can be a very large number easily.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, there's a bit of disconnect here. Not everyone is a giant powerful creature of doom. A siren shouldn't be suddenly a powerful, large combatant. Adding Lair to Size makes no sense here. Not all monsters make sense to gain bonus Defense or Initiative, as they're not a swift form. Gaining bonuses to social and intelectual abilities is likewise very strange in a number of cases. Just... why? Also, adds Lair to resistance rolls twice?<br /> <br /> Fourth, this mechanically not that different from simply spending the required Satiety to empower your abilities. The only benefit is &quot;flashing&quot; your form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to reread the sections on this, but what I can say upfront is that I have been powerfully underwhelmed by the abilities of the Beast in our current game. Especially in his Horror form which, IMO, really does not inspire the sphincter spilling horror a terrible Yeti monster should inspire, especially compared to that of some other starting splats (Werewolves and Demons, to name the primary two). Which would not be such an issue in my eyes were they not specifically intended for crossover","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T16:59:04-07:00","id":701415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701409#post701409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to reread the sections on this, but what I can say upfront is that I have been powerfully underwhelmed by the abilities of the Beast in our current game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This tells nobody anything. Give details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially in his Horror form which, IMO, really does not inspire the sphincter spilling horror a terrible Yeti monster should inspire, especially compared to that of some other starting splats (Werewolves and Demons, to name the primary two). </div> </div> </div>All of their purchased powers can be used for free and the Horror uses more than your strongest Attributes unless you toss all your bonus dots into Size.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which would not be such an issue in my eyes were they not specifically intended for crossover </div> </div> </div>The point of the crossover aspect of Beast is not to be Bigger And Badder Than Every Other Monster right out of the gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T17:09:18-07:00","id":701424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701415#post701415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This tells nobody anything. Give details.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I said I have to reread, I haven't given it a really good look since the 1st draft, where I was so profoundly annoyed that I admittedly did some skimming. I'm not about to engage in frivolous debate until I have slightly better ground to debate on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T03:45:46-07:00","id":701916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701409#post701409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Going Loud is a good comparison, a terrible idea, but there if you need it.</div> </div> </div> </div> While Going Loud is a rough comparison, its a fundamentally flawed one. When you Go Loud, you can still put a secondary Cover on after the scene ends. This is equivalent to Going Loud with removing all your aether and destroying all your covers at once, becoming automatically Burned, do not pass go, do not collect 200 dollars. And, even then, its a simple matter for one of your ring-mates to offer a quick and easy pact to share bits of their Cover to hide you - there's no equivalent for that in Beast. A more apt comparison is a werewolf hitting Harmony 0 and the packmates trying to force him back to some semblence of balance every time he falls into Kuruth.<br /> <br /> In Beast, you have two options - derail the current plot for a session or two while you try to desperately nurse a teammate back to health while under seige of hunter/heroes, or let the PC die. Now, while fun once in a while, enforcing it with any regularity is going to remove the tension of hitting Ravenous (which is detrimental to the game), and it will get old hat quick. Its like the occasional feeding scene in vampire - good in moderation, but quickly gets stale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll have to reread the sections on this, but what I can say upfront is that I have been powerfully underwhelmed by the abilities of the Beast in our current game. Especially in his Horror form which, IMO, really does not inspire the sphincter spilling horror a terrible Yeti monster should inspire, especially compared to that of some other starting splats (Werewolves and Demons, to name the primary two). Which would not be such an issue in my eyes were they not specifically intended for crossover </div> </div> </div> Which specific abilities (and what level are you maintaining Satiety at)? Atavisms are roughly on par with vampire physical Disciplines, and are far more exp efficent. And what &quot;in Horror form&quot; are you talking about? Merging with your Horror at Low Satiety adds a rather notable bump in power. Weak has absolutely not been the experience myself and many others have encountered in game (I'm playing a water-based dragon type), so I'm kind of curious where you're running into these issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701424#post701424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I said I have to reread, I haven't given it a really good look since the 1st draft, where I was so profoundly annoyed that I admittedly did some skimming. I'm not about to engage in frivolous debate until I have slightly better ground to debate on.</div> </div> </div> </div> Frivolous debate? Putting aside the opposition-based stance you're implying here, this isn't a debate. This is about feedback and understanding where others are coming from, not to prove each other right or wrong.<br /> <br /> It does sound like you have a few misunderstandings, which is a different matter entirely. I do have to agree with Satchel that it sounds like you want the Beasts to be Bigger and Badder right out of the gate, which is actually not what the game is meant to support at all. So, I want to know where you're coming from, because knowing you, that doesn't quite sound right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T10:23:07-07:00","id":702293,"title":"","content":"So what would you guys suggest as a third bowl of porridge option here? Do the current rules allow you to manifest what you really are in any way that lets you travel more than 5 feet out your own door? I've been skimming back over the rules but nothing is jumping out at me yet for making a giant a real giant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8508-phaide","name":"Phaide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T10:44:04-07:00","id":702298,"title":"","content":"Incarnation, as mentioned. It's kind of an endgame option though, as also mentioned.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of this is mitigated by the simple fact that you should be playing sometime in the Lair, where you around in full form anyways. Like the balance of Kinship and Hunger, a good game of Beast finds a balance of nightmarish dissonance in the real world and mythic actualization in the Lair.<br /> <br /> It's more rewarding, for me, to have the variety, and at any rate, being a full blown giant raven or wolf is more fun in a psycho-spiritual landscape that bends to my presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T12:37:54-07:00","id":702442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=702293#post702293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would you guys suggest as a third bowl of porridge option here? Do the current rules allow you to manifest what you really are in any way that lets you travel more than 5 feet out your own door? I've been skimming back over the rules but nothing is jumping out at me yet for making a giant a real giant.</div> </div> </div> </div> A &quot;Primordial Pathway&quot; Style merit or bonus dice. When you use the rules to open a Primordial Pathway, you turn into the Horror and everyone can see it. As it stands, all supernaturals can already see the beast as they really are, so that's a moot point. The primary reason for this rule is to flash your real self to mundane mortals, and the system is already in place, if a bit difficult to pull off at times do to the odd dice pool. There's no reason to reinvent the wheel here.<br /> <br /> Remember that this is the World of Darkness, and we don't want you to be able to run around Times Square as a full out dragon to have cameras pick you up. So, leaving past your front door (ie opening the door to the Lair) is a major Masquerade breach. We want to keep things restricted as to keep the monsters in the shadows. The previous posters are trying to use Ravenous as a balancing point, but that is just problematic. Ravenous means the rule is restricted to life/death situations as a kind of last ditch effort. As I said above, the whole point of the rule is to flash your true form to mortals, and generally mortals (even of the hunter/hero variety) are rarely threats enough to justify its use at this point. The presented rules completely misses the point of creating the house rule in the first place!<br /> <br /> Well, except in Pendragon's case, because it seems that she's (he's?) interested in a frenzy mechanic because of some dice pools that poster feels are too low. Which is a different matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T14:13:13-07:00","id":707378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=702298#post702298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incarnation, as mentioned. It's kind of an endgame option though, as also mentioned.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of this is mitigated by the simple fact that you should be playing sometime in the Lair, where you around in full form anyways. Like the balance of Kinship and Hunger, a good game of Beast finds a balance of nightmarish dissonance in the real world and mythic actualization in the Lair.<br /> <br /> It's more rewarding, for me, to have the variety, and at any rate, being a full blown giant raven or wolf is more fun in a psycho-spiritual landscape that bends to my presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say nothing of the fact that you can always figure out ways to force the situation to transition to your Lair ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;Primordial Pathway&quot; Style merit or bonus dice. When you use the rules to open a Primordial Pathway, you turn into the Horror and everyone can see it. As it stands, all supernaturals can already see the beast as they really are, so that's a moot point. The primary reason for this rule is to flash your real self to mundane mortals, and the system is already in place, if a bit difficult to pull off at times do to the odd dice pool. There's no reason to reinvent the wheel here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also just take the 'Behold, My True Form!' Nightmare and reveal your Horror to hapless victims while causing damage to them at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T18:51:10-07:00","id":707929,"title":"","content":"How about taking the form allows you to access one Incarnate ability for the duration? That would give you a big boost to your physical prowess for the duration and may cause a character to seek out an Inheritance as they get a taste of what true power is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2553-kai","name":"Kai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2553_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T19:29:31-07:00","id":708039,"title":"","content":"Incarnation is more than simply becoming a fleshy-shapeshifter. So, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T17:55:34-08:00","id":778001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack?p=701173#post701173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I miss this when it was posted? Regardless I like it, I was already considering something like this and yours is a good jumping point. So I'll be using it, slightly tweaked.<br /> <br /> Tweaked Version:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Mythic Form </b><br /> In times of great stress, great need, or great hunger Beasts can shed their human body to become living embodiment of horror they have inside themselves. Albeit at great cost. To invoke this form the Beast must expend all her remaining Satiety, taking the Ravenous Condition, and cannot gain further Satiety for the remainder of the scene. Beasts who expend all their Satiety normally are at risk of assuming this form involuntarily. Any time a Beast with the Ravenous Conditions encounters a stimulus for their Hunger they must roll their remaining unspent willpower points, on a failure they assume their Mythic Form.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: In Mythic Form a Beast becomes the physical embodiment of her internal soul. Her true form and Atavisms become visible to onlookers, while her human body fades from sight. While in this form the Beast uses her Mythic Traits* (see note below), and treats all Atavisms as though she had spent Satiety to power them. However, this power comes at a price. For one the Beast must simplemindedly pursue her Hunter, ignoring all other interests. This isn't like Death Rage or Frenzy, the Beast retains her sentience, ability to reason, plot and even converse, but she cares for nothing save the sating of her thirsts. Second, the Beast becomes a magnet for Heroes, like a sixth sense heroes from all over the land will feel the pull to hunt her. Mythic Form lasts until the end of the scene, or until the Beast flees into her Lair.<br /> <br /> *<b>Note</b>: Further hacks modify the Beast's True Form with the following statistics:<ul><li>The Horror, instead of gaining [Lair * 2] points to spend between her Attributes and size, adds her Lair dots to all Dice Pools, her Size, Defense, Initiative, and Speed. Applies her full defense vs Firearms, and cannot suffer Conditions that make no sense in her new form, like Arm Wrack on a giant snake. (No longer must Beasts labor under dubious to downright embarrassingly low dice pools)</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, I really need to get my hands on the latest draft of the kickstarter, since some of the stuff being mentioned is rather new. Anybody willing to send me a copy?<br /> <br /> That said, the Horror/Mythic Form can definitely round out the Begotten's arsenal by providing a way to let out the Beast within for devastating effect. Though I probably would make a few changes. One, maybe they could still regain Satiety even after assuming the Form, but they could probably suffer a penalty (equal to half their dots, rounded down, perhaps?) in the feeding roll, and may not even be able to change back voluntarily unless they rise back up to Medium Satiety. Alternatively, we could go with something like the Soul Shocked Condition, wherein successes in rolling your current Satiety translate to a number of points you still keep past the transformation.<br /> <br /> As for the Beast acting as a magnet for Heroes, that could perhaps be reflected as Heroes having an automatic success (or even exceptional success) in detecting him/her via Heroic Tracking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}